<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'><head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>Legal Draft</title></head><body>LEGAL CONTRACT / AGREEMENT<br><br>TITLE: Legal Notice – Breach of Service Contract dated 10 January 2026<br>DATE: 2/21/2026<br><br>BETWEEN: [PARTY A] AND [PARTY B]<br><br>WHEREAS the parties desire to enter into this agreement regarding: My client, Ms. Ayesha Khan (Resident of Lahore), entered into a Web Development Service Agreement with Mr. Ali Ahmed on 10 January 2026.<br><br>As per the agreement, the respondent agreed to develop and deliver a fully functional e-commerce website within 30 days for a total consideration of Rs. 150,000.<br><br>An advance payment of Rs. 75,000 was made via bank transfer at the time of signing the agreement.<br><br>Despite multiple reminders and expiry of the agreed deadline, the respondent has failed to deliver the website and has stopped responding to communications.<br><br>This conduct amounts to breach of contract, causing financial loss and inconvenience to my client.<br><br>Draft a formal legal notice demanding:<br>1. Immediate completion of the project within 7 days; OR<br>2. Refund of the advance payment of Rs. 75,000.<br><br>Mention that failure to comply will result in initiation of legal proceedings under applicable contract laws of Pakistan.<br>Use professional and formal legal language.<br><br>TERMS AND CONDITIONS:<br>1. COVENANTS: The parties agree to the specifications provided in the case facts.<br>2. VALIDITY: This contract is binding upon execution.<br><br>IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the parties have signed this Agreement.<br><br>SIGNATURES:<br><br>____________________          ____________________</body></html>